},[18,1656,1636],{},[36,1658,1659],{},"command -v \u003Cname>",[36,1661,1662],{},"which",") to check if a command exists — ",[36,1665,1666],{},"command -v"," is POSIX, built into the shell, and respects functions\u002Faliases. ",[36,1669,1662],{}," is an external command and misses shell functions.",[42,1672,1673,1637,1675,1678],{},[18,1674,1636],{},[36,1676,1677],{},"hostnamectl"," on systemd distros — shows distro, kernel, arch, hostname, and chassis type in one command.",[42,1680,1681,1684,1685,1688,1689,1692,1693,1696],{},[18,1682,1683],{},"Performance",": ",[36,1686,1687],{},"strace -c \u003Ccmd>"," reveals syscall counts — if a tool makes 10,000 ",[36,1690,1691],{},"stat"," calls, switching to a buffered alternative (like ",[36,1694,1695],{},"find -maxdepth 1",") can be 100x faster.",[42,1698,1699,1702,1703,1706],{},[18,1700,1701],{},"Portability",": Alpine uses musl, not glibc — binaries compiled against glibc (most prebuilt Linux binaries) won't run on Alpine without ",[36,1704,1705],{},"gcompat"," or a musl build. This bites Docker users pulling glibc binaries into Alpine images.",[23,1708,1710],{"id":1709},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[39,1712,1713,1731,1751,1767,1793,1820],{},[42,1714,1715,1722,1723,1726,1727,1730],{},[18,1716,1717,602,1719,1721],{},[36,1718,1008],{},[36,1720,1018],{}," are virtual",": they exist in RAM, not on disk. ",[36,1724,1725],{},"du -sh \u002Fproc"," reports 0 or errors. Don't back them up. Writing to ",[36,1728,1729],{},"\u002Fproc\u002Fsys"," changes live kernel state — typos can crash the system.",[42,1732,1733,1738,1739,1742,1743,1746,1747,1750],{},[18,1734,1735,1737],{},[36,1736,131],{}," is not a regular file",": it's a character device. ",[36,1740,1741],{},"cp realfile \u002Fdev\u002Fnull"," doesn't \"save\" the file — it discards it. ",[36,1744,1745],{},"cat \u002Fdev\u002Fnull > bigfile"," truncates ",[36,1748,1749],{},"bigfile"," to 0 bytes (a common idiom).",[42,1752,1753,1758,1759,1762,1763,1766],{},[18,1754,1755,1757],{},[36,1756,998],{}," is cleared on reboot"," (and sometimes hourly by ",[36,1760,1761],{},"systemd-tmpfiles","): don't store anything you need to keep. Use ",[36,1764,1765],{},"\u002Fvar\u002Ftmp"," for files that survive reboots (up to 30 days by default).",[42,1768,1769,1775,1776,1779,1780,160,1782,1784,1785,1788,1789,1792],{},[18,1770,1771,1774],{},[36,1772,1773],{},"$SHELL"," is your login shell, not necessarily your current shell",": if you run ",[36,1777,1778],{},"zsh"," from ",[36,1781,79],{},[36,1783,1773],{}," still says ",[36,1786,1787],{},"\u002Fbin\u002Fbash",". Use ",[36,1790,1791],{},"ps -p $$ -o comm="," for the current shell.",[42,1794,1795,1684,1804,1807,1808,1811,1812,1815,1816,1819],{},[18,1796,1797,1800,1801],{},[36,1798,1799],{},"uname -r"," vs ",[36,1802,1803],{},"uname -a",[36,1805,1806],{},"-r"," gives only the kernel release (",[36,1809,1810],{},"6.8.0-31-generic","), which is what ",[36,1813,1814],{},"apt install linux-image-$(uname -r)"," expects. ",[36,1817,1818],{},"-a"," includes hostname, kernel name, etc.",[42,1821,1822,1825,1826,1706],{},[18,1823,1824],{},"Alpine uses musl, not glibc",": binaries compiled against glibc (most prebuilt Linux binaries) won't run on Alpine without ",[36,1827,1705],{},[23,1829,1831],{"id":1830},"quick-quiz","🧠 Quick Quiz",[14,1833,1834,1835,1838,1839,1842],{},"You run ",[36,1836,1837],{},"man passwd"," and see the command documentation. You actually wanted the format of ",[36,1840,1841],{},"\u002Fetc\u002Fpasswd",". What went wrong, and how do you fix it?",[1844,1845,1846,1850,1870,1886],"details",{},[1847,1848,1849],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1851,1852,1854,1855,1858,1859,1863,1864,1858,1866,1869],{},[36,1853,1837],{}," defaults to the lowest-numbered section with a match — section 1 (user commands), the ",[36,1856,1857],{},"passwd"," ",[1860,1861,1862],"em",{},"command",". The ",[36,1865,1841],{},[1860,1867,1868],{},"file format"," is in section 5. Fix it with:",[77,1871,1872],{"language":79},[28,1873,1875],{"className":82,"code":1874,"language":79,"meta":34,"style":34},"man 5 passwd\n",[36,1876,1877],{"__ignoreMap":34},[87,1878,1879,1881,1883],{"class":89,"line":90},[87,1880,1590],{"class":106},[87,1882,1593],{"class":110},[87,1884,1885],{"class":117}," passwd\n",[14,1887,1888,1889,1892,1893,1896,1897,1900,1901,1904,1905,1908,1909,1912,1913,1916,1917,1920],{},"This is the section-number syntax: ",[36,1890,1891],{},"man \u003Csection> \u003Cname>",". When a name exists in multiple sections, always specify the section to avoid ambiguity. Other common pairs: ",[36,1894,1895],{},"man 1 crontab"," (command) vs ",[36,1898,1899],{},"man 5 crontab"," (file), ",[36,1902,1903],{},"man 2 open"," (syscall) vs ",[36,1906,1907],{},"man 1 open"," (if a command named ",[36,1910,1911],{},"open"," exists), ",[36,1914,1915],{},"man 8 mount"," (admin command) vs ",[36,1918,1919],{},"man 2 mount"," (syscall).",[1922,1923,1924],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}",{"title":34,"searchDepth":97,"depth":97,"links":1926},[1927,1928,1931,1934,1938,1939,1940,1941,1944,1945,1946],{"id":25,"depth":97,"text":26},{"id":60,"depth":97,"text":61,"children":1929},[1930],{"id":183,"depth":103,"text":184},{"id":324,"depth":97,"text":325,"children":1932},[1933],{"id":440,"depth":103,"text":441},{"id":464,"depth":97,"text":465,"children":1935},[1936],{"id":586,"depth":103,"text":1937},"Edge Case: Merged \u002Fusr on Modern Distros",{"id":681,"depth":97,"text":682},{"id":893,"depth":97,"text":894},{"id":1068,"depth":97,"text":1069},{"id":1392,"depth":97,"text":1393,"children":1942},[1943],{"id":1488,"depth":103,"text":1489},{"id":1628,"depth":97,"text":1629},{"id":1709,"depth":97,"text":1710},{"id":1830,"depth":97,"text":1831},"Linux is a monolithic kernel managing CPU, memory, devices, and process scheduling. Combined with GNU userspace tools, a display server, and applications, it forms a Linux distribution. This chapter covers the kernel–userspace boundary, syscall mechanics, the FHS, and the virtual filesystems that make Linux a unified system — through the lens of production code and edge-case behavior.","md",{},"\u002Flinux\u002F01-introduction-and-architecture",{"title":5,"description":1947},"linux\u002F01-introduction-and-architecture","eRuIaU-cmGNtKpoBYatYv-AVu9OjcVos8OESfLKnNrM",1789140923234]